ice method?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c> <think>\nCertainly! The lattice method is an alternative way to multiply numbers using a grid. Let's use the numbers 994 and 801 to demonstrate this method.\n\nHere are the steps:\n\n1. **Set up the lattice grid:**\n   - Draw a 2x2 grid because we are multiplying a 3-digit number by a 3-digit number.\n   - Label the top row with the digits of 994 (9, 9, 4) and the left column with the digits of 801 (8, 0, 1).\n\n   ```\n     9 | 9 | 4\n   \u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\n     8 |   |   |\n   \u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\n     0 |   |   |\n   \u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\n     1 |   |   |\n   ```\n\n2. **Multiply each digit in the top row by each digit in the left column:**\n   - Multiply 9 by 8, 9 by 0, and 4 by 1, and write the results in the corresponding cells of the grid, splitting the tens and units digits.\n\n   ```\n     9 | 9 | 4\n   \u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\n     8 | 72| 0 |\n   \u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\n     0 | 0 | 0 |\n   \u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\n     1 | 9 | 4 |\n   ```\n\n3. **Add the numbers in each diagonal, carrying over if necessary:**\n   - Start from the bottom right and move to the top left.\n   - Add the numbers in the diagonals: 4 + 0 = 4, 0 + 9 = 9, 72 + 0 + 1 = 73.\n\n   ```\n     9 | 9 | 4\n   \u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\n     8 | 72| 0 |\n   \u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\n     0 | 0 | 0 |\n   \u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\n     1 | 9 | 4 |\n   ```\n\n4. **Combine the results:**\n   - The final result is read from the top left to the bottom right.\n\n   ```\n     9 | 9 | 4\n   \u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\n     8 | 72| 0 |